   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The inner expression is \\( u = 4 x^{2} - \\frac{9}{2} \\), with \\( u' = 8 x \\), and \\( \\frac{d}{du}\\arcsin u = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "inverse trigonometric derivative with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = \\frac{8 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(4 x^{2} - \\frac{9}{2}\\right)^{2}}} + 2 x \\arcsin{\\left(4 x^{2} - \\frac{9}{2} \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = -1, \\( u = - \\frac{1}{2} \\) and \\( u' = -8 \\), so \\( h'(-1) = \\frac{\\pi}{3} - \\frac{16 \\sqrt{3}}{3} = - \\frac{16 \\sqrt{3}}{3} + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\).",
